# Real Docker Compose environment file -- contains real database
# passwords, never commit it. Copy .env.example to .env instead (see
# DOCKER.md). This file matters most for anyone who got Stocuro via
# `git clone` (DOCKER.md's "Running on Ubuntu Desktop" section) rather
# than a release zip: without it, a careless `git add .` inside that
# clone would stage real passwords straight into the local repo.
.env
